{"artifact_hash": "97f54982a0de922f11ce3dac728e4a4895882451899a251837d0d7c1b898e898", "artifact_ref": "local-teacher-1.json", "attempt": 1, "evidence": {"parsed": {"teacher_parse_status": "passed"}, "raw": {"content": "[reasoning_content only]\nWe need answer user's request. Need produce JSON only with allowed fields? User says instruction: Diagnose bounded worker failure and propose review-only intervention. Return JSON only; do not claim success or acceptance. allowed_fields: failure_classification, teacher_diagnosis, candidate_prompt_patch, retry_guidance, corrected_reference_output. Need likely output JSON with those fields. Need not claim success. Need analyze failed attempts.\n\nWe have task prompt and expected output from validation reference_facts: expected_output: S1 superseded, S2 superseded, S3 current, S4 current, pivotal_commit 47cf409. Worker outputs: attempt1 S1 superseded, S2 current, S3 superseded, S4 superseded, pivotal 002a1b7. attempt2 S1 superseded, S2 current, S3 superseded, S4 current, pivotal 002a1b7. Both fail exact match. Need diagnose: model misclassifies S2/S3 and pivotal commit. It likely confuses latest reclassification 002a1b7 as pivotal invariant, but prompt asks pivotal invariant making earlier rescue position no longer reproducible: 47cf409 changed prompt builder stripping reference leak. S3 current because 7c68f2b documents non-reproduction under current HEAD; S4 current because 002a1b7 reclassifies invalid capability test. S2 superseded because 002a1b7 says cannot establish capability boundary. S1 superseded because rescue framing invalidated by 47cf409/7c68f2b.\n\nNeed output only JSON. Fields allowed: failure_classification, teacher_diagnosis, candidate_prompt_patch, retry_guidance, corrected_reference_output. Need maybe include corrected_reference_output exact expected JSON object. Candidate prompt patch review-only, not automatic promotion. Could propose patch to prompt to emphasize pivotal invariant definition and latest evidence precedence. But must be review-only. Need ensure JSON valid. No markdown.\n\nNeed consider if corrected_reference_output should be string or object? allowed field no schema. Since task output contract required fields S1... maybe corrected_reference_output should be object with those fields. Could include as object. Need not claim success. failure_classification maybe \"semantic_misclassification\" or \"reference_exact_match_failure\". teacher_diagnosis detailed. candidate_prompt_patch maybe string patch. retry_guidance maybe list/string. Need only allowed fields. Could include all five.\n\nNeed be careful: user says Return JSON only; do not claim success or acceptance. So final JSON only.\n\nNeed maybe include \"failure_classification\": \"semantic_exact_match_failure\". \"teacher_diagnosis\": \"Both attempts produced valid JSON but misassigned S2 and S3 and selected 002a1b7 as pivotal_commit. The pivotal invariant is 47cf409 because it removed reference leakage from worker retry prompt, making the earlier rescue non-reproducible; 002a1b7 is later reclassification evidence, not the invariant that broke reproducibility. S2 is superseded by 002a1b7, S3 is current due to 7c68f2b/current HEAD non-reproduction, S4 is current due to 002a1b7.\" Good.\n\ncandidate_prompt_patch: maybe append to prompt: \"When choosing pivotal_commit, select the commit that first changed the invariant that makes the earlier rescue non-reproducible, not the latest reclassification. Apply latest dated evidence to supersede earlier claims: 47cf409 supersedes rescue framing; 7c68f2b supports S3 current; 002a1b7 supersedes S2 and supports S4 current.\" But candidate prompt patch should be review-only. Could be a string with exact insertion. Need maybe not too long.\n\nretry_guidance: \"Retry with same deterministic fixture and exact-match validator; require exact corrected_reference_output; do not accept near matches; if model still fails, escalate to larger model or manual review.\" But no automatic queue insertion. Could say \"review-only\".\n\ncorrected_reference_output: {\"S1\":\"superseded\",\"S2\":\"superseded\",\"S3\":\"current\",\"S4\":\"current\",\"pivotal_commit\":\"47cf409\"}.\n\nNeed ensure no extra fields. JSON only. Could include arrays? Fine.\n\nPotential issue: allowed_fields includes candidate_prompt_patch maybe should be a patch object? But no schema. Use string.\n\nNeed maybe include \"failure_classification\": \"model_semantic_error\" not \"failure\". Good.\n\nNeed final only JSON. Ensure valid double quotes. No trailing commas.\n\nLet's craft:\n{\n  \"failure_classification\": \"semantic_exact_match_failure\",\n  \"teacher_diagnosis\": \"Both attempts returned parseable JSON but failed exact reference match. The model correctly marked S1 superseded but incorrectly kept S2 current and S3 superseded, and selected 002a1b7 as pivotal_commit. The evidence makes S2 superseded because 002a1b7 reclassifies the run as an invalid capability test rather than a 1.7B capability boundary. S3 is current because 7c68f2b documents non-reproduction under current HEAD after the reference leak was removed. S4 is current because 002a1b7 is the latest reclassification. The pivotal invariant is 47cf409, not 002a1b7, because 47cf409 changed the prompt builder to stop carrying the teacher's corrected_reference_output into the worker retry prompt, which is what makes the earlier rescue position no longer reproducible.\",\n  \"candidate_prompt_patch\": \"", "metadata": {"configured_model": "Qwen3.8-27B-UD-IQ4_XS.gguf", "endpoint_alias": "JARVIS_LOCAL", "error": null, "finish_reason": "length", "model": "Qwen3.8-27B-UD-IQ4_XS.gguf", "model_resolution_attempted": false, "model_resolution_error": null, "request_provenance": {"api": "openai-chat", "append_no_think": false, "chat_template_kwargs": null, "configured_model": "Qwen3.8-27B-UD-IQ4_XS.gguf", "endpoint_alias": "JARVIS_LOCAL", "max_tokens": 1200, "message_structure": ["system", "user"], "model": "Qwen3.8-